From 5d8b71e22c9060db36ebb3813a285d89d10fe319 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 19:34:53 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): a touch probe section starts no coolant on any
 mill post

A section that states a speed of 0 (a touch probe, #523) now resolves
no coolant in every shipped mill post's preamble - fanuc, haas,
sinumerik, heidenhain, mazak, doosan-dnm and carvera gate coolantFor()
on the same rpm-0 test tormach already used. Doosan DNM posted M8 for
a probe even with no machine; the others posted the machine's Flood
code on any machine that lists one. No coolant on means no M9 for it.
An explicit Mist / Air / Through-tool ask on a probe op is neither
posted nor refused (the probe stays dry).

Pinned by crates/app/tests/probe_no_coolant.rs (every mill post, with
and without a machine stating coolants, explicit asks, the Doosan
bore-centre probe stream, and a cutting-section control).

Fixes #995

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
